 "note": "Busselton Volunteer Fire and Rescue station, between Albert St, Stanley Pl and Cammilleri St (OSM way 370721434). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and a 2019 Mapillary view of its west side. A tan face-brick hall under a terracotta tile gable roof, the ridge running back from Albert St, two roller doors for the appliances in the gable end onto the concrete apron, a small flat-roofed entry block beside them, flat-roofed wings to the west (with the brick screen wall and the covered parking slab) and to the south. The roof is drawn about 20 x 21 m (in life about 21 wide by 19 deep) so the ridge runs front to back: specHouse ridges the longer side. Sign is plain lettering only and its wording is a guess. Metres: x left to right as seen from Albert St (east to west), y back from the front wall.",
